# 0112 WIP: EP2 Bulk OUT (RX) Stage A, counters and diagnostics only.
#
# 0111 closed the bulk IN log pipe: 3719 consecutive packets with no gaps
# and no duplicates.  This version adds the missing OUT direction without
# touching the TX GPD ring, buffers, queue, timing or EP0 path.
#
# RX follows the vendor mtu3_qmu model and the P9 probe values:
#   - 16 pre-armed GPDs with one 64-byte buffer each (P9 uses 4; the deeper
#     ring is headroom for bursts while the 1 ms poll drains);
#   - RX GPD layout: dw0 high 16 = buffer capacity, dw3 low 16 = actual
#     received length filled by hardware, dw3 high 8 = buffer/next high
#     address bits (TX stores those in dw0, so the layouts are different);
#   - RX2CSR1 = RX_SLOT(2) | bulk, RX2CSR2 = RX_FIFOADDR(0) | 512-byte
#     segments, QCR0 RX checksum enable, QCR3 ZLP/COZ and RQERRIESR0/R1;
#   - completion uses RQCPR2/RQHIAR2 plus HWO, then the GPD is re-armed;
#   - no RX watchdog: a bulk OUT with no host data has no done by design.
#
# QISAR1 is shared between TX and RX.  The existing TX code used to clear
# every QISAR1 bit; it now clears only TXQ_EMPTY/CS/LEN, leaving RXQ_EMPTY/
# CS/LEN/ZLP for the RX poll.  There is no echo and no change to the TX
# data path.  Vendor request 0xC0/0x23 is read-only RX telemetry: packet
# count, bytes, ZLP count, last length, FNV-1a checksum, RQCPR/RQHIAR,
# RQCSR, QISAR0/1, RQERRIR0/1, errors, RXQ_EMPTY and the 36-bit ext-bad
# counter.
#
# Acceptance: host writes 1/15/63/64/65/128-byte payloads and (if the host
# stack emits it) a ZLP; the diag counts, last length and cumulative FNV
# match; RQERRIR0/1 stay zero and ext_bad stays zero; a burst longer than
# the ring may NAK/retry but must not stall or drop the device; then rerun
# the 0111 TX stream and require >=100 consecutive packets, no gaps or
# duplicates, recoveries=0.

MACOS_VERSION=13.5
KERNEL_CONFIG=DEVELOPMENT
MACHINE_CONFIG=SWEET

BASE_REPO=https://github.com/MakrSas/ios-topaz.git
BASE_SHA=5095ac19dbdcf37b64b81fe443f4027ad51b84bf
PATCHSET_SHA256=0071fbec58188fefdcd9f92406a3b2b3d8c234714fef0a94a994d6136bda807e
BASELINE_CHANGES_SHA256=1edb66332bb4daa8b1abcd6c4de77a0e88ed9c7e9bb4a2a7045a2696e53ab338

DXB_REPO=https://github.com/blacktop/darwin-xnu-build
DXB_SHA=663906528d1cd5ea8fde7de6f16de73db9511549

KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA=
CI_RUN_ID=
CI_KERNEL_SHA256=
CI_KERNEL_EXEC_DATA_SHA256=
CI_IMAGE_SHA256=

BOOT_CMDLINE=config/0112-boot.cmdline
